      "writtenOn": "2024-03-05T18:58:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Logic to remove a flag can follow the rules. There could be 6 combinations of the flag.\nFlag condition:\n1) True:\na) Flag is the only condition \u003d\u003e Just remove the if check. i.e. \n```\nif(FLAG) \n   { // some code }\n else \n   { // else block code } \n```\n   will look like post flag removal \n```{ // some code } ```\n\nb) Flag with additional conditions:\ni) AND: e.g\n```\nif (FLAG \u0026\u0026 OTHER_CONDITION)\n  { // some code }\nelse\n  { // else block code }\n```\nwill result in\n```\nif (OTHER_CONDITION) \n  { // some code } \nelse\n  { // else block code }\n```\nii) OR condition\n```\nif ( FLAG || OTHER_CONDITION )\n { // some code }\nelse\n  { // else block code }\n```\nwill result in removal of the if check and the else block \u003d\u003e\n```\n{ // some code }\n```\n\n2) False :\na) Flag is the only condition \u003d\u003e Remove the entire code within the if block and the \n\n```\nif(!FLAG) \n   { // some code }\n else \n   { // else block code } \n```\n   will look like post flag removal \n```\n   { // else block code } \n```\nb) Flag with additional conditions:\ni) AND: e.g\n```\nif (!FLAG \u0026\u0026 OTHER_CONDITION)\n  { // some code }\nelse\n  { // else block code }\n```\nwill result in\n```\n   { // else block code } \n```\n\nii) OR condition\n\n```\nif ( !FLAG || OTHER_CONDITION )\n { // some code }\nelse\n  { // else block code }\n```\nwill result in removal of the if check and the else block\n```\nif (OTHER_CONDITION) \n  { // some code } \nelse\n  { // else block code }\n```\n\nThough, I agree if there are nested condition operators it can get confusing and error prone.\n\nI will go ahead and make the changes to reflect your request.",
